GPU: use the JM21/SM6225 A610 nominal clock as the Spes default.

The FiiO JM21 port is the closest public A610 reference for this phone: it
keeps the GPUCC/GDSC/SMMU path on the stock khaje power sequence and explicitly
does not enable its optional overclock in the public build.  Spes already has
the corresponding Zonda PLL and RPM rail code; its default was still the
19.2-MHz bring-up clock, which made a payload without an explicit boot argument
fall back to the diagnostic baseline.  Select the validated 785-MHz nominal
corner by default, while retaining 19/300/600/785/1025/1115 as explicit
diagnostic choices and leaving the higher clocks opt-in.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -1327,3 +1327,3 @@
 	 */
-	uint32_t gpu_mhz = 19, gfx_cfg = 0;
+	uint32_t gpu_mhz = 785, gfx_cfg = 0;
 	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("spesgpu_mhz", &gpu_mhz, sizeof(gpu_mhz));
